  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nLab\nglyphfield\n\n// Experiment\n\nglyphfield \n\nDraws any picture as source code on a canvas. It runs the portrait at the top of this site.\n\nView the repo\nstars\n1,260\ndownloads\n9,400\nlicense\nMIT\nInstall\nCopy\nnpm install glyphfield\n\n\nREADME.md\nMIT\n\nglyphfield draws any picture as text on a canvas. It samples the light of the image per cell and sets one glyph from the text you give it, brighter cells first. The portrait at the top of this site runs on it.\n\nUsage\nts\nCopy\nimport { glyphfield } from \"glyphfield\"\n\n\n\nconst field = glyphfield(canvas, {\n\n  image: \"/portrait.webp\",\n\n  text: source,       // any string, it repeats\n\n  cell: 9,            // px\n\n  ink: \"#F1F2EC\",\n\n})\n\n\n\nfield.reveal()        // glyphs settle once\n\nNotes\nOne canvas, no dependencies, 2.4 kB\nPauses when it is off screen or the tab is hidden\nRespects reduced motion: it draws the final frame and stops\n\nThe image must be served from the same origin, or with CORS headers, because the pixels are read.\n\nIn this readme\n\n01\nUsage\n02\nNotes\nKind\nExperiment\nLicense\nMIT\nRepository\ngithub.com\nMore from the lab. \n06\nEverything in the lab\nLibrary · 890 stars\ntinyflip\nLayout animations in 1.1 kB, using the FLIP technique and nothing else.\nTool · 640 stars\na11y-probe\nA command line check that tabs through your page and tells you where focus got lost.\nTool · 410 stars\ntokens-to-css\nTurns a design token file into typed CSS custom properties, with dark mode built in.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
